-- title:
--   Retraction reads the forgetful chart map as p-th power
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \neq 0$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and assume $p \mid M$, $p^2 \nmid M$, and that every unit of $\mathbb{Z}/M$ mapping to $1$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ lies in $H$; assume also that the Laurent series $q^{-1}\,j_{\mathrm{num}}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ lies in the field $\mathrm{qExpFunctionFieldC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,\top$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight. For the subgroups `ΓN p M H hpM` and `ΓM M H` of $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$, write $\mathcal{O}_N$ and $\mathcal{O}$ for the corresponding $j$-finite chart rings, i.e. the elements of the respective $q$-expansion function fields integral over the $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-subalgebra generated by $j$, where $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)} = R\,p$. Let $\iota_0 : \mathcal{O}_N \to \mathcal{O}$ be a $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-algebra map preserving the underlying Laurent series, and $\vartheta$ a $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-algebra automorphism of $\mathcal{O}$ such that the series of $\vartheta(\iota_0 b)$ is the series of $b$ with $q$ replaced by $q^p$ (substitution of exponents by multiplication by $p$). Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$, residue field $\kappa$ algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and $\rho : \mathbb{Z}_{(p)} \to A$ a ring map compatible with the structure map to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, so that $\kappa$ is a $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-algebra via $\mathrm{res} \circ \rho$. Then for any pair $\sigma_0, \sigma_1$ of $\kappa$-algebra maps $\kappa \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}} \mathcal{O} \to \kappa \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}} \mathcal{O}_N$ with $\sigma_0 \circ (\mathrm{id} \otimes \iota_0) = \mathrm{id}$ and $\sigma_1 = \sigma_0 \circ (\mathrm{id} \otimes \vartheta)$, one has $\sigma_1(1 \otimes \iota_0 b) = (1 \otimes b)^p$ for every $b \in \mathcal{O}_N$.
--
--   This is the chart-ring form of the statement that, on the second component of $X_H(M)$ in characteristic $p$, the forgetful map down to level $M/p$ is the relative Frobenius, in the shape used for the two-chart integral model at a place of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ above $p$. It feeds the identification of the degeneracy map on that component with Frobenius and the construction of the generic chart of the model at $p$, via [`ModularCurve.XHDRLevel.comp_one_comp_fibreMap_ne_id_of_theta_iota0_eq_qExpand_of_liesOverPrime`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRLevel.comp_one_comp_fibreMap_ne_id_of_theta_iota0_eq_qExpand_of_liesOverPrime), [`ModularCurve.XHDRLevel.exists_chart_frobenius_comp_one_fibreMap_pi_of_liesOverPrime`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRLevel.exists_chart_frobenius_comp_one_fibreMap_pi_of_liesOverPrime) and [`ModularCurve.exists_xHDRModelAtP_atkinLehner_generic_chart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_xHDRModelAtP_atkinLehner_generic_chart).
